---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title={"Skydaze Privacy Policy - PiFl Labs"}
  description={"PiFl Labs Skydaze (하늘멍) privacy policy — no account, ads or analytics SDKs; location is used only on the device and coordinates are never sent to a server."}
  canonical="https://pifl-labs.com/en/apps/pipi-sky/privacy/"
  alternates={[{"hreflang":"en","href":"https://pifl-labs.com/en/apps/pipi-sky/privacy/"},{"hreflang":"ko","href":"https://pifl-labs.com/ko/apps/pipi-sky/privacy/"},{"hreflang":"ja","href":"https://pifl-labs.com/ja/apps/pipi-sky/privacy/"},{"hreflang":"x-default","href":"https://pifl-labs.com/ko/apps/pipi-sky/privacy/"}]}
  extraCss={["/styles.css"]}
>
<section class="legal-hero">
        <div class="container">
            <a href="/en/" class="legal-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Home</a>
            <h1><i class="fas fa-shield-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i> <span class="text-gradient">Skydaze Privacy Policy</span></h1>
            <p class="legal-date">Effective: October 30, 2026</p>
        </div>
    </section>
    <main class="legal-page">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="legal-card">
                <p>Skydaze does not collect account information, advertising identifiers, contacts, photos, microphone data, or usage analytics. The app includes no advertising or analytics SDKs.</p>
                <h2>Location</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>Location permission is used only to choose nearby sky-data tiles and calculate the positions of the Sun and Moon.</li>
                    <li>The app does not convert your location into a precise address. It downloads one common data bundle for every region, so no coordinates or location-specific request is sent to the server. Only the selected region name (outside Korea, a 1° grid cell about 100 km across) is stored on your device for the next launch; precise coordinates are not stored.</li>
                    <li>If you deny permission, the app uses your saved region or the sky around the main city of your device's time zone.</li>
                </ul>
                <h2>Information stored on your device</h2>
                <p>The app stores only the following on your device: heading calibration, red night mode, sky-gazing sound preference, background music choices and any music files you add, music repeat mode and chosen tracks with their play order, larger-controls preference, app language choice, sky time reminder choices and the reminders scheduled from them, onboarding completion, whether you have seen the first-run height-rail hint, selected region name, a review request record (the number of days you used the app for two minutes or more, the last day counted and the time used that day, and the app version in which a review was last requested), and a cached copy of the sky-data bundle. Music files you add are only copied inside the app and never sent anywhere. Sky time reminders are scheduled and shown on your device only; no server is involved. Deleting the app also deletes this information.</p>
                <h2>Sharing</h2>
                <p>Because Skydaze does not collect personal information, it does not share or sell personal information to third parties. Share this sky hands a picture of the sky on screen, with its source line, to your device's share sheet, and you choose where it goes. The app never sends the picture to a server and puts no coordinates in the picture or its text. The picture stays briefly in the app's temporary folder for sharing and is cleared by the device. Saving to Photos is done by your device's share sheet; Skydaze never reads your photos.</p>
                <h2>Children</h2>
                <p>Skydaze does not collect personal information and does not knowingly request personal information from children.</p>
                <h2>Contact</h2>
                <p>For privacy questions, email <a href="#" data-email-user="support" data-email-domain="pifl-labs.com"><span class="email-text">support (at) pifl-labs.com</span></a>.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>
</BaseLayout>
